**`[ASSUMED]` Class B decisions, for one-pass human override**

1. `IExtractionIngestWorkflow` declares only the members T04 implements.
   `architecture.md` sketches classification-override and duplicate-resolution
   on this interface, but T05 owns those policies and does not own this file;
   declaring them here would leave an unimplemented contract, which rule 2
   forbids. They belong on `IExtractionReviewWorkflow`.
2. Two read members ship here (`GetDocumentAsync`, `GetCaseAsync`). T06 needs
   "the two read surfaces" and no other task's file list declares a read
   contract; projecting in the portal would be the UI deriving state. Both are
   implemented and tested in this pass, which also keeps `ExtractionProjection`
   genuinely consumed.
3. `ExtractionWorkflowOptions.ProviderCallLimit` is the one configured value —
   a fail-closed bound on one provider call, never a quality signal, and not a
   confidence bound. No confidence bound exists anywhere in this feature.
4. Classification and extraction each take their own content lease, because the
   port documents that a provider consumes the stream once from its current
   position. Nothing seeks or buffers source bytes in the coordination module,
   and every lease is disposed before the operation returns.

**Gate unchanged.** T04 ships no HTTP route, no UI component, no registration in
the composition root, no migration, no production content reader, no production
document-intelligence provider, no correction or acceptance path, no review
record, and no deployment authorization. Each belongs to a later task.
